5d\" already exists` error recurring on every single subsequent test's setup since then — `TestLayerDownloadErrorsBounded` at 23:22:28 is now the 11th consecutive test in this run to collide with the same stuck name (after `TestCPUPlacementWholeCoreSMT`, `TestCPUPlacementMultiApp`, `TestCPUPlacementStability`, `TestCPUPlacementParkedSiblings`, `TestCPUPlacementNeedsRepack`, `TestCPUPlacementFailsClosed`, `TestCPUIsolatedPool`, `TestVMAppPurgeAfterPowerCycle`, `TestLotsOfApps`). Live checks confirm the pattern: `evetest status` shows \"No EVE devices found\" and `evetest sdn status` reports \"SDN client is not initialized\" — the harness's own failure-path teardown ran cleanly locally, but the orphaned Proxmox VM 111 itself was never removed. Per `live-ledger.md`, this exact \"VM deletion timeout → stale device blocks same-named recreation\" signature has no prior occurrence in past nightly runs, so it's a new manifestation of the broader known class of Proxmox broker/VM-lifecycle flakiness, first seen tonight at 23:11:40, not a previously-documented recurring issue — and it will keep failing every remaining test in the suite until VM 111 is manually cleared on the Proxmox broker host.","time":{"start":1795212602000,"stop":1795212661450,"duration":59450}},{"uid":"69f243d8f43eaac5","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/27/#testresult/69f243d8f43eaac5","status":"passed","time":{"start":1795131965000,"stop":1795132171260,"duration":206260}},{"uid":"7a63bd9ad2abc86e","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/25/#testresult/7a63bd9ad2abc86e","status":"passed","time":{"start":1795039947000,"stop":1795040204810,"duration":257810}},{"uid":"489924524e80d729","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/23/#testresult/489924524e80d729","status":"passed","time":{"start":1794953131000,"stop":1794953345730,"duration":214730}},{"uid":"3ec4b95e484701f2","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/21/#testresult/